=
- ```tabular
+ ```tabular

- column  Reason
- column  Means
- row  `Dns`  the host's name could not be resolved
- row  `Refused`  the host refused the connection
- row  `Ssl(reason)`  the TLS layer could not be established; its own reason is `Handshake`, `Key`, `Peer` or `Protocol`
- row  `Timeout`  the server did not respond within the time limit
- row  `Unknown`  the failure was not recognized as one of the others
+ column  Motivo
+ column  Significa
+ row  `Dns`  no se pudo resolver el nombre del host
+ row  `Refused`  el host rechazó la conexión
+ row  `Ssl(reason)`  no se pudo establecer la capa TLS; su propio motivo es `Handshake`, `Key`, `Peer` o `Protocol`
+ row  `Timeout`  el servidor no respondió dentro del tiempo límite
+ row  `Unknown`  el fallo no se reconoció como ninguno de los demás

= row  `Unknown`  the failure was not recognized as one of the others
- ```
+ ```

- A TLS failure is therefore told apart from a network failure, and its reason says at which stage
- it happened. An expired certificate, a certificate for the wrong host, a revoked certificate, a
- broken cipher suite and an undersized Diffie–Hellman group are each refused during the
- handshake. The client is tested against the [badssl.com](https://badssl.com/) collection of
- deliberately broken endpoints, so each refusal is verified.
+ Así, un fallo de TLS se distingue de un fallo de red, y su motivo dice en qué etapa ocurrió. Un
+ certificado caducado, un certificado para otro host, un certificado revocado, un conjunto de
+ cifrado roto y un grupo Diffie–Hellman demasiado pequeño se rechazan cada uno durante el
+ handshake. El cliente se prueba con la colección [badssl.com](https://badssl.com/) de endpoints
+ rotos a propósito, de modo que cada rechazo está verificado.

- Sometimes a connection must be made to a host whose certificate cannot be validated, such as a
- development server with a self-signed certificate. A relaxed `TlsAcceptance` in scope permits it.
- Accepting an unvalidated certificate is then a decision that can be found by searching the code
- for the import.
+ A veces hay que conectarse a un host cuyo certificado no puede validarse, como un servidor de
+ desarrollo con un certificado autofirmado. Una `TlsAcceptance` relajada en el ámbito lo permite.
+ Aceptar un certificado no validado es entonces una decisión que puede encontrarse buscando la
+ importación en el código.

